{
  "id": "pioneer-ddj-sb",
  "name": "DDJ-SB",
  "vendor": "Pioneer DJ",
  "ports": [
    "DDJ-SB"
  ],
  "evidence": "Captured from a DDJ-SB on Windows 11 (WinMM) on 2026-11-17 with the midi_probe example: every control moved once, about 27 000 messages. A control with verified false was not moved on that side; its number comes from the other deck.",
  "notes": [
    "Faders, knobs, EQ and filters are 14-bit: CC n carries the high 7 bits and CC n + 0x20 the low 7.",
    "Buttons send Note On 0x7F when pressed and Note On 0x00 when released.",
    "Jogs are relative, centred on 64. Touching the top sends note 0x35; turning it sends CC 0x23, the side CC 0x21. The scale of 0.0025 s a step assumes 720 steps a turn and is not yet measured.",
    "Both tempo faders on the unit tested move by themselves (steps of 48 to 64 out of 16383, about once a second), hence the dead band.",
    "SHIFT is handled by the controller: pads send other notes while it is held.",
    "Master and headphone level are analog, on the audio interface, and send no MIDI.",
    "The FILTER knobs drive the colour effect, so connecting selects Filter on both channels.",
    "The FX buttons were given Beat FX, slip and reverse by curado; the hardware prints no names for them."
  ],
